    "done_when": "First, the worker searches tests/ for an existing test that already drives this whole path: dispatch, a worker killed by a signal, a classification of interrupted naming the signal, a resume, and completion. If one exists, the manifest names it (file and test), explains how it covers each step, commits nothing, and reads complete. Otherwise, a new tests/test_a_killed_worker_resumes_to_completion.py drives that path with a stub worker in a temporary repository and crew home. It asserts, in order: the classification reads interrupted, the recorded signal is named, the run is offered for resume, and the resumed attempt's manifest completes promotion. The named negative control (make recovery ignore the exit record's signal) turns the interrupted-with-signal assertion red. The gate is the new file plus tests/test_crew_recovery.py, tests/test_direct_resume_needs_an_observed_death.py and tests/test_crew_launch_failure.py, run with -n 8 at base and at head. Both suite arms are recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder, and each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id. Basetemps go under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and the worker deletes every directory it created there before status complete, printing what it deletes and listing it in artifacts. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/worker-death-is-recorded/a-killed-worker-resumes-to-completion.html records the result. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete.",
